{"name":"Cotinga Purple","hex":"#340059","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cotinga","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the neotropical passerine birds of the family Cotingidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotinga"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotinga","blocks":[{"text":"The cotingas are a large family, Cotingidae, of suboscine passerine birds found in Central America and tropical South America. Cotingas are birds of forests or forest edges, that are primarily frugivorous. They all have broad bills with hooked tips, rounded wings, and strong legs. They range in size from 12–13 cm (4.7–5.1 in) of the fiery-throated fruiteater up to 48–51 cm (19–20 in) of the Amazonian umbrellabird."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Cotingidae_diversity.jpg/330px-Cotingidae_diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotinga","wikidata":"Q647533"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ampelioides_tschudii_%28Frutero_escamado%29_%2824%29_%2814148007464%29.jpg/500px-Ampelioides_tschudii_%28Frutero_escamado%29_%2824%29_%2814148007464%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ampelioides_tschudii_%28Frutero_escamado%29_%2824%29_%2814148007464%29.jpg/1280px-Ampelioides_tschudii_%28Frutero_escamado%29_%2824%29_%2814148007464%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ampelioides_tschudii_%28Frutero_escamado%29_%2824%29_%2814148007464%29.jpg/500px-Ampelioides_tschudii_%28Frutero_escamado%29_%2824%29_%2814148007464%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmpelioides_tschudii_(Frutero_escamado)_(24)_(14148007464).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pipreola_frontalis_squamipectus.jpg/500px-Pipreola_frontalis_squamipectus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pipreola_frontalis_squamipectus.jpg/1280px-Pipreola_frontalis_squamipectus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pipreola_frontalis_squamipectus.jpg/500px-Pipreola_frontalis_squamipectus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe